[[ ## yaml_spec ## ]]
description: |
  An 8-bit ALU with a registered output. Every cycle it applies one of eight operations, selected by op, to the unsigned operands a and b, and registers the 8-bit result together with a zero flag and a carry flag.
tech_node: SkyWater 130HD
clock_period: 2.5ns
ports:
- {name: clk, direction: input, type: wire, description: Clock input (rising edge)}
- {name: reset, direction: input, type: wire, description: 'Synchronous reset (active high) - clears result, zero and carry.'}
- {name: a, direction: input, type: '[7:0]', description: First operand (unsigned)}
- {name: b, direction: input, type: '[7:0]', description: Second operand (unsigned)}
- {name: op, direction: input, type: '[2:0]', description: Operation select (see operations)}
- {name: result, direction: output, type: 'reg [7:0]', description: Registered 8-bit result}
- {name: zero, direction: output, type: reg, description: 'Registered flag, 1 when the result is 0'}
- {name: carry, direction: output, type: reg, description: Registered carry / borrow / shifted-out bit (see operations)}
module_signature: |
  module alu_8bit(
      input            clk,
      input            reset,
      input      [7:0] a,
      input      [7:0] b,
      input      [2:0] op,
      output reg [7:0] result,
      output reg       zero,
      output reg       carry
  );
operations: |
  op    name  result                              carry
  000   ADD   (a + b) mod 256                     1 if a + b > 255 (carry out of bit 7)
  001   SUB   (a - b) mod 256                     1 if a < b (borrow), unsigned compare
  010   AND   a & b                               0
  011   OR    a | b                               0
  100   XOR   a ^ b                               0
  101   SHL   (a << 1) mod 256                    a[7] (the bit shifted out)
  110   SHR   a >> 1 (logical, MSB becomes 0)     a[0] (the bit shifted out)
  111   SLT   1 if a < b (unsigned), else 0       0
  zero = 1 exactly when the 8-bit result is 0 (for every operation).
sample_input: op=ADD a=200 b=100 -> op=SUB a=5 b=7 -> op=SLT a=3 b=9 -> op=SUB a=9 b=9
sample_output: result=44 zero=0 carry=1 -> result=254 zero=0 carry=1 -> result=1 zero=0 carry=0 -> result=0 zero=1 carry=0
timing: |
  result, zero and carry are registered: they are updated at each rising edge (latency 1).
  sample_output[i] is the value of the outputs right after the rising edge that samples
  sample_input[i]. During reset all three outputs are 0.
  Race-free testbench: drive a, b and op on a falling edge, check the outputs on the next
  falling edge.


